K. Balak! You have recited the sacred verses of the Padma Purana with devotion and emotion.

From the roots, the small pebbles, and the tiny ants,
The Shila Sutapati, the devotees,
The Paliti Penindi, who are immersed in devotion,
Are all present here. [
](https://www.jkp.com/us/content/padma-purana-hindu-scriptures) 

This excerpt is from the Padma Purana, a Hindu scripture. It is a prayer to the Shila Sutapati, the deity of the pebbles, and is recited with devotion and emotion. The verses describe the presence of the deity in the form of small pebbles, ants, and devotees. The Paliti Penindi are the devotees who are immersed in devotion. This excerpt is a beautiful example of the poetic language used in Hindu scriptures. It is a reminder of the presence of the divine in all forms of life and the importance of devotion and emotion in connecting with the divine. [
